{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784911559,"nonce":"kIudnyYZBTdHHIrurfMWMCf4JzE=","title":"engine: tick fault isolation + bounded per-run dead-letter (ADR-0059)","message":"One poison run can abort a whole scheduler tick: admit/advance and most reconcile* still ?-propagate errors, so a single bad run stalls all runs in that tick. Additionally, errors swallowed by reconcile_services' collect-and-continue (scheduler.rs:914-917) can hot-loop unbounded with no dead-letter bound.\n\nADR-0059 is Accepted-as-Proposed with only the reconcile_services collect-and-continue landed. Build: (1) isolate per-run failures in admit/advance/reconcile* so one run's error doesn't abort the tick; (2) a bounded per-run dead-letter for repeatedly-failing runs (mirror the outbox poison bound). The one open engine-correctness item from the 2026-07-24 unimplemented sweep.","files":null}]}